From 1c73046443b3c7c3347c8f80469b8708cadaca97 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 23:21:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: a setting for what wakes the computer from sleep

Linux lets no USB device wake a computer from sleep but the keyboards of
the boot protocol, which usbhid arms by itself. The IR receiver that a
home cinema PC is used with (a flirc, a Media Center receiver) could not
wake it, and a PC that does not wake looks hung (issue 32 of LibreELEC
Hades). hades-wake (packages/sysutils/hades-wake) now arms the receivers
of remote controls by default, and this is its setting.

System > Sleep > "Wake from sleep" chooses what may wake the computer
besides its power button: "Remotes" (the default: the receivers of remote
controls, and the keyboards that the kernel arms by itself), "Remotes and
keyboards" (also every other keyboard, and a receiver that a keyboard
shares with a mouse or a touchpad) or "Only the power button". Mice and
game controllers never wake it. The choice is one word in
/storage/.cache/hades-wake (no file for the default), written beside it
and renamed over it, and read back; hades-wake reads it at each start,
for each device plugged in and after each sleep, and is run here at once
("apply"), so a change needs no restart. What it says goes to the log of
Kodi, and a notification says the choice and how many USB devices may
wake the computer. Where hades-wake cannot run, the choice is kept and
holds from the next start, and that is said. The list has the choice in
force preselected, which is what Kodi answers when something else closes
it. Hidden where hades-wake is not there or the computer cannot sleep (no
freeze and no mem in /sys/power/state).

Tested on the host (tools/regress/boot, stage wakesettings), with the
add-on of the recipe and every patch applied with -F0, and stand-ins for
Kodi: 47 checks (the strings in the four languages, defaults.py, the group,
when it is shown, every answer of the list, a file that cannot be written,
a hades-wake that fails); with this patch reversed it fails. Not run in
Kodi.
